<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario 3/5: the canonical override example from
     semantic_bridge_to_owl.md §10. BaseType declares Mandatory "Part" :
     PartType. SubType <: BaseType overrides "Part" : AdvancedPartType (a
     genuine subtype of PartType).

     Expect VT(SubType, "Part") to carry BOTH edges simultaneously:
       - rdfs:subClassOf opcua:AdvancedPartType   (§8, the override)
       - rdfs:subClassOf VT(BaseType, "Part")     (§9, which is itself
         rdfs:subClassOf opcua:PartType)
     This dual-edge pattern is what lets a DL reasoner flag a *contradictory*
     override (see test_vt_contradiction) while leaving a *consistent* one
     (this file, since AdvancedPartType really is a PartType) satisfiable. -->
